      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Originalist proponents strongly justify their approach by emphasizing democratic legitimacy; they argue that the framers' intent provides a stable, authoritative baseline for law. A core argument is that if the meaning constantly shifts, the Constitution loses its prescriptive force. Living constitutionalists counter that rigidly adhering to 18th-century understandings ignores changing social realities, arguing that the right to self-defense must adapt to modern threats and lifestyles. They contend that constitutional interpretation should serve current justice rather than merely serve history.",
      "source": "target",
