    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that. Looking at the weight of the arguments, though—it seems like the originalist perspective provides a much more concrete, text-based framework for the law, whereas the living constitutionalist view seems a bit more subjective and dependent on whoever is interpreting it at the time. Do you think the originalist approach is fundamentally more robust for maintaining the rule of law?",
