      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While the originalist approach offers undeniable textual stability, its robustness is often challenged by its rigidity when confronting novel circumstances. Its strength lies in predictability, which is foundational to the rule of law, as it limits judicial discretion. However, critics argue that an overly narrow originalism can fail to protect fundamental rights against evolving societal harms. Ultimately, whether it is \"more robust\" depends on whether one prioritizes legal certainty or adaptive justice.",
